Date: Sun, 27 Sep 2026 12:23:48 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 50/55] Drone tracks: a kit's drone rows saved after its other
 rows, for firmware before v16

A song's rows refer to their kit's drums by index in the file. Firmware before v16 skips
<droneTone>, so a drone row's drum among the others moved every later row onto its
neighbour's drum and left the last one without a drum (getDrumFromIndex() falls back to the
first, a duplicate); saved there, for good.

When saving a song, Kit::writeDataToFile() now writes the drums in two passes, the others
first and the drone rows' last, each in the rows' order as before. The remaining drums (those
without a row in the clip the order comes from) are taken out of the list as they're written
as well, so the list is rebuilt in the file's order and v16's drumIndex stays consistent.
Older firmware then loses only the drone rows. A kit preset has no rows referring to its
drums and keeps the rows' order. Songs without drone rows save the same XML as before
(tests/song SAVE=1: same sha256).

Test: mastertune tests/song/drone_edit_emu.py (run.sh DRONE=1): a gate row between drone
rows is saved first, each row still refers to its own drum.

